BT 1 0 0 1 0 47.5 Tm /F3+0 10.1 Tf 14.4 TL (Panel A shows conspecific share conditional on an egg being fertilised. The share increases when heterospecific sperm lose function faster, remains constant when) Tj T* (half-lives are equal, and decreases when heterospecific sperm persist longer. Panel B shows the probability that a potential egg is fertilised at all. That probability) Tj T* (declines in every scenario because both functional stores decline. For the one-day heterospecific half-life, conspecific share reaches about 94% at day eight, while) Tj T* (total fertilisation falls to about 6%. Both quantities are required to interpret the biological consequence of a paternity bias.) Tj T* ET
